    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm putting together a nutrition plan for a client who wants to max out hypertrophy. can you give me a technical breakdown of how leucine specifically triggers the mTOR pathway and how staying in a caloric surplus impacts their nitrogen balance? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a potent signal by directly stimulating the mTORC1 complex to phosphorylate downstream effectors like S6K1 and 4E-BP1, which are essential for activating protein synthesis. This process can be thought of as fueling the anabolic machinery, requiring adequate caloric surplus to support the high energy costs of muscle building. Simultaneously, a caloric surplus improves nitrogen retention by providing the necessary substrate and regulatory conditions for the body to silence protein breakdown, effectively shifting nitrogen balance into a positive state. This creates the optimal environment where increased nitrogen accretion directly translates into net muscle hypertrophy for your client.",
